      "text": "1. **Social-based reels** — stage: starting out (~3K followers). Client-proof and live social proof; side-angle/interview style, filmed with real students/clients (Zoom works). Growth: poor. Buyer intent: high — these get the first $10-20K months. Boostable with simple ads.\n\n2. **Achievement-based reels** — stage: multiple six figures. Income milestones and growth indicators as credibility scaffolding (\"how I went from 0 to...\"), standing-format, any decent location. Growth: decent (people love numbers). Buyer intent: decently high. Retire the number-leading once proof exists — numbers are early-stage scaffolding. **Pulsify note:** milestones framed on student results wherever possible; own-revenue claims only when verifiable.\n\n3. **Demonstration reels (Miro-style)** — the transformation-on-a-screen format: a system, belief, or framework shown technically (screen share + board). Desk + laptop production. Growth: excellent while the format variant is fresh. Buyer intent: excellent. The format that built the source's brand; saturates fastest — needs the invention pipeline behind it.\n\n4. **Authority-pairing clips** — stage: ~70-100K/month. Stage talks, podcasts (own or guest), masterminds, in-person client events, team-in-content — clipped into distributable moments. \"Just providing value isn't enough\" at this stage. Growth: can spike massively (the brand-making 1.1M-view podcast). Production: easy once credibility opens doors.\n\n5. **Talking head (raw)** — stage: established credibility. Strategy breakdowns and insider systems ONLY — broad talking heads go viral and buy nothing. Camera on, idea sharp, post. Growth: modest. Buyer intent: excellent. This is the sophistication-inversion play: max-raw at max-credibility."
