      "title": "The reel format ladder: The ladder (stage -> format)",
      "tags": [
        "reel",
        "short",
        "format",
        "content"
      ],
      "text": "6. **Proof-of-positioning clips** — podcast-style credibility moments and client-result clips that \"reconfirm\" everything prior; world-view content, not how-to. Often lives on the second/proof account. Growth: slow but viral-capable. Buyer intent: excellent.\n\n7. **Reach-based reels** — stage: industry leader. Maximum distribution on niche-specific topics (never generic routines/motivation): contrarian takes, conviction to camera, institutional validation, cinematic allowed here. Growth: the fastest (100K -> 139K followers in ~2 months). Buyer intent: deliberately lower — this is the \"hot audience\" manufacturing phase.\n\n8. **Vlog-style conversion content** — the harvest after a reach spike: behind-the-scenes niche stories (the fired-setter arc), systems + massive pain shown. Views intentionally drop ~5x; conversions spike (\"this is the actual strategy\"). Growth: good. Buyer intent: maximum. **Pulsify register:** BTS of real work, not lifestyle.\n\n**The alternation:** reach phases (7) make the audience hot; conversion phases (8 + stories) harvest it. Judge each phase by its own metric — views in reach, attributed DMs/calls in conversion — never one by the other's."
