      "text": "The three-step build:\n\n1. **Find the agreed belief** — what the prospect already tells themselves (\"I just need better habits and more grinding\").\n\n2. **Reframe it** so agreeing with the old belief becomes impossible (\"You've never made a conscious decision in your life, ever\").\n\n3. **The induced conclusion** does the selling (\"I need to rewire my identity, not just my habits\") — which is precisely what the offer delivers.\n\nDeployment rules:\n- ONE reframe per brand era, repeated consciously and unconsciously across all content, until the market associates it with the creator. Not five reframes; one.\n- The repetition multipliers govern patience: the creator hears it 10x more than clients, ~50x more than a cold viewer. Boredom is the signal it's starting to land, not the signal to change.\n- Every piece of content passes the stimulation test: \"does it stimulate people to use my mechanism?\" — mostly indirectly."
