      "title": "The content operating rhythm: The two clocks",
      "tags": [
        "cadence",
        "posting",
        "schedule",
        "week",
        "routine",
        "consistency"
      ],
      "text": "- **Daily clock:** offer and delivery iterate every day — \"your offer, your delivery changes all the [ __ ] time.\" These are living assets tuned to each client.\n- **Quarterly clock:** acquisition systems and content formats run in ~3-6 month structures, then get reinvented (format invention pipeline). Do not tinker with the format weekly; run it, measure it, reinvent it on schedule.\nConfusing the clocks is a top failure: people reinvent formats weekly (never compounding) and leave offers static (never improving)."
